.TH CRUMB 1 "October 2026" "crumb 1.0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crumb \- self-hosted agent harness and natural-language terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crumb
.RI [ --resume " session-id" ]
.br
.B crumb exec
.RI [ options ] " request"
.br
.B crumb completions
.RI shell
.br
.B crumb mcp serve
.SH DESCRIPTION
Crumb is an interactive shell with an optional supervised agent runtime.
Ordinary shell commands work without an AI provider. Agent execution remains
subject to the user's configured permissions and approval policy.
.PP
The Debian build reads provider credentials from environment variables. It
does not include native desktop keyring support or remote Sigstore marketplace
verification.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B /help
Display the interactive command reference.
.TP
.B /version
Display the installed Crumb version.
.TP
.B /exit
Leave Crumb.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/crumb/
Per-user configuration and credential references.
.TP
.I .crumb/
Project-local state, policies, skills, and session data.
.SH SECURITY
Crumb does not allow a model to grant itself additional permissions. Review
requested commands and workspace changes before approving them. Report private
security issues using the process in the upstream SECURITY.md file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR bash (1)
.PP
Project documentation: https://crumb.elixpo.com
